    "narrative": "Our core engine today centers on the middle infield, where **Gunnar Henderson** (77.16) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) offer the highest efficiency floors. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Yesavage, carrying a +14% dynamic platoon boost that makes him our must-start anchor. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a breakout performance against Kelly; the combination of a high-leverage order spot and the favorable park factor elevates his expected production into the elite category. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.32) remains a top-tier play as well, leveraging a +18% SP skill boost against Young, despite a slight platoon penalty.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the scarcity of our stolen base profile. **Nasim Nunez** (60.80) secures a spot in the UTIL slot over higher-base options like **Josh Jung** (44.49) because of the game-state variables: Kelly\u2019s slow delivery creates a high-upside environment for **Nasim Nunez** to hunt bags, which is prioritized given our 5x5 scarcity requirements. Conversely, **Josh Jung** was the odd man out; despite a decent projection, the matchup against the left-handed Messick coupled with the higher ceiling of our other infielders forced him to the bench. \n\nRisks remain on the periphery, particularly with our outfield deployment. **Andy Pages** (48.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (51.36) both face Detmers, an elite arm (3.21 xERA) that suppresses their overall output. While **Kyle Tucker** is too talented to bench, the negative SP skill adjustments highlight a lower-than-usual expected output for our power-speed anchors. We are cautiously optimistic that the +2% speed-related boost for **Andy Pages** against a slow-working Detmers will allow for at least one successful theft, maintaining our edge in the SB category while we navigate these tougher pitching matchups.",
